    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d718">

                <pb facs="0750" n="746" xml:id="pg746"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">898.24/548: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Peck</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chungking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-03-30T13:00:00+07:00">March 30, 1939—1
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received March 30—11:30 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>227. Reference Embassy’s telegram 216, March 28, 10 a.m.<anchor n="49"
                        xml:id="d718-f1"/> The Embassy learns from an informed Chinese source that
                    Sun Fo’s<anchor n="50" xml:id="d718-f2"/> mission to Moscow is to plead with
                        Stalin<anchor n="51" xml:id="d718-f3"/> with whom he is on good terms for
                    the granting of additional Russian support to China in the form of arms and
                    munitions, and especially military aircraft the maintenance of the average
                    number of which the Chinese authorities hope to increase from a present total of
                    200 to 500 available planes. The same source [apparent omission] Sun is [to?]
                    proceed in about 2 weeks to Paris and London for discussions along similar lines
                    with French and British officials.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Peiping.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Peck</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d718-f1" n="49" xml:id="d718-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d718-f2" n="50" xml:id="d718-f2-content">
                <p>President of the Chinese Legislative Yuan.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d718-f3" n="51" xml:id="d718-f3-content">
                <p>Josif V. Stalin, Secretary General of the Communist Party in the Soviet
                    Union.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
